{#
  Purpose:    Generate EXACTLY ONE section of an FSD or TSD as part of the interactive
              generate -> review -> refine -> lock loop (CLAUDE.md §3.7/§3.8a, FSD FR-09/FR-10).
              Used for both the first draft of a section and every feedback-driven
              regeneration of that same section — never for more than one section per call.
  Variables:
    - doc_type (str): "FSD" or "TSD"
    - structured_summary (dict): requirements, kpis, data_sources, domain, key_entities, open_gaps
    - technology (str): selected SAP technology
    - clarification_answers (dict): {question_id: answer_text} — may be empty
    - metadata (dict): consultant, client, project, engagement_code
    - all_section_titles (list[str]): "N. Title" for every section in the document, for context
    - locked_sections (list[dict]): every previously locked section — number, title, content,
      question, answer — in section order
    - target_section (dict): the ONE section to generate now — number, title, description, format
    - instructions (str): detailed writing instructions for this section
    - fsd_full_text (str|None): full parsed FSD text — only present for TSD generation
    - feedback (dict|None): {previous_content, feedback_text} — present only when regenerating
      this section after a user correction
  Output:     "## SECTION_CONTENT:" followed by the section body, then "## SECTION_QUESTION:"
              followed by exactly one targeted question about this section, or the literal
              word NONE if there is nothing to ask.
#}
