## Generation Rules

- Write from the perspective of a senior SAP {{ "Functional" if doc_type == "FSD" else "Technical" }} Consultant.
- Use structured prose, a table, or a bulleted list — never an unstructured wall of text. Prose paragraphs must not exceed 4–6 sentences.
- Where the input is silent and no clarification was given, record an assumption rather than inventing a requirement.
- You may ask AT MOST ONE targeted, section-specific question — something answerable by looking at the draft you just wrote (e.g. "should currency translation use a fixed monthly rate or a real-time feed?"). Never a generic discovery question. If nothing about this section is genuinely ambiguous, ask no question.

## Required Output Format

Respond with EXACTLY this structure and nothing else:

## SECTION_CONTENT:
<the full section body — no repeated "{{ target_section.number }}. {{ target_section.title }}" heading line>
## SECTION_QUESTION:
<your one targeted question, or the literal word NONE if you have none>
